$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Method C : (S)-BINAP (96 mg, 0.15 mmol) and AgOTf (41 mg, 0.15 mmol.)
were sheltered from light and stirred in dry THF (1.5 mL) for 15 minutes.
A solution of sorbaldehyde (55 μL, 0.5 mmol.) in dry THF (0.5 mL) was
then added. The resulting mixture was cooled down to -20°C and
allyltributyltin (0.16 mL, 0.51 mmol.) was added. The solution was
stirred at -20°C for 20h, and then quenched with 1N HCl (2.5 mL) and KF
(0.5 mg). The slurry was stirred for another 4h until a white precipitate
was formed. The latter was filtered on a pad of silica and washed with
Et2O (50 mL). The filtrate was dried over MgSO4, filtered and
concentrated in vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography to afford 50 mg of the desired alcohol (72%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
