$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for preparation of dienyl
alcohols. To a cooled solution (-78oC) of dienal (1 equiv) in THF (5
mL/mmol of dienal) was added the appropriate Grignard reagent (1.5
equiv). After addition, the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min, and
then quenched by the addition of satd. aqueous NH4Cl (ca 3 mL/mmol
dienal). The resulting solid was removed via filtration and washed with
Et2O (ca. 3 x 5 mL permmol of dienal). The water phase was extracted with
Et2O (ca. 3 x 2 mL per mmol of dienal). The combined organic phases were
dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatograph on silica (ethyl acetate/hexane= 1:9, v/v). Dienyl alcohol.
IIa. According to the general procedure, (E,E)-2,4-decadienal (1.0 g, 6.5
mmol) was treated with methylmagnesium bromide (3.2 mL, 3.0 M in ether,
9.8 mmol) in THF (30 mL). IIc. According to the general procedure,
2,4-hexadienal (1.00 g, 10.4 mmol) is treated with isopropylmagnesium
bromide (7.8 mL, 2.0 M in THF, 15.6 mmol) in THF (50 mL) to give
2-methyl-octa-4,6-dien-3-ol (IIc, 1.24 g, 85%) as colorless oil: 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) 6.13-6.20 (m, 1H), 5.98-6.10 (m, 1H), 5.64-5.74 (m, 1H),
5.56 (dd, 7.3, 15.1 Hz, 1H), 3.85 (dd, 6.6, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.75 (d, 6.9 Hz,
3H), 1.69-1.74 (m, 1H), 1.47 (br s, 1H), 0.93 (d, 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.89 (d,
6.9 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) 131.7, 131.6, 130.9, 129.5, 77.9,
34.0, 18.2, 17.9; IR (neat) 3388, 2958, 2929, 2872, 986; HRMS (EI, m/z)
calcd for C9H16O (M+) 140.1201, found 140.1196 m/z.
