$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for preparation of dienyl alcohols. To a cooled
solution (-78oC) of dienal (1 equiv) in THF (5 mL/mmol of dienal) was
added the appropriate Grignard reagent (1.5 equiv). After addition, the
reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min, and then quenched by the
addition of satd. aqueous NH4Cl (ca 3 mL/mmol dienal). The resulting
solid was removed via filtration and washed with Et2O (ca. 3 x 5 mL
permmol of dienal). The water phase was extracted with Et2O (ca. 3 x 2 mL
per mmol of dienal). The combined organic phases were dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated. The residue was purified by flash chromatograph on silica
(ethyl acetate/hexane= 1:9, v/v). Dienyl alcohol. IIa. According to the
general procedure, (E,E)-2,4-decadienal (1.0 g, 6.5 mmol) was treated
with methylmagnesium bromide (3.2 mL, 3.0 M in ether, 9.8 mmol) in THF
(30 mL). Undeca-3,5-dien-2-ol (IIa, 982.8 mg, 90%) as colorless oil: 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 6.16 (dd, 10.6 Hz, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 6.01 (dd, J = 10.6
Hz, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 5.63 (dt, 7.1 Hz, 14.7 Hz, 1H), 5.55 (dd, 6.6 Hz, 15.2
Hz, 1H), 4.25 (dt, 6.1 Hz, 12.6 Hz, 1H), 2.72 (br s, 1H), 2.03 (dd, 7.1
Hz, 14.7 Hz, 2H), 1.33 (dt, 7.1 Hz, 14.1 Hz, 2H), 1.22-1.29 (m, 4H), 1.21
(d, 6.1 Hz, 3H), and 0.85 (t, 7.1 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3)
135.0, 134.6, 129.6, 129.3, 68.2, 32.4, 31.2, 28.7, 23.3, 23.1, 13.8; IR
(neat) 3353, 2924, 2860, 1457, 1134, 1060, 987; HRMS (EI, m/z) calcd for
C11H20O (M+) 168.1514, found 168.1507.
