$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3Z-4,8-Dimethylnona-3,7-dien-2-ol (6c2): To a solution of neral5 (6c1)
(5.10 g, 0.0336 mol) in ether (150 mL), MeLi (29 mL, 0.0436 mol, 1.5 M in
ether) was added at -78 °C. After stirring at the same temperature for
1.5 h, 1 N HCl was added slowly. The organic phase was separated and the
aqueous phase was further extracted twice with ether. The combined
organic layer was washed with water and brine, dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated to give a residue, which was purified by silica gel flash
chromatography (AcOEt/hexane, 1/20) to give 6c2 (5.46 g, 0.0329 mol; 98%)
as colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 5.15 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 1H), 5.04 (t,
J = 5.7 Hz, 1H), 4.41-4.48 (m, 1H), 1.98-2.06 (m, 4H), 1.64 (s, 3H), 1.62
(s, 3H), 1.53 (s, 3H), 1.23 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ
136.2, 131.1, 129.1, 122.8, 63.0, 31.1, 25.3, 24.4, 22.3, 22.0, 16.4; IR
(neat, cm-1): 3345; EI-MS m/z 168 (M+); EI-HRMS Calcd for C11H20O (M+):
168.1514, Found: 168.1512.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Challenge toward Structural Complexity Using Asymmetric Catalysis:
