$DATUM To a stirring -78°C solution of t-BuOK in THF (104 mL, 1.0 M in THF, 104
mmol) was added via cannula trans-2-butene (11.7 g, 0.21 mol) followed by
the addition of n-BuLi (41.8 mL, 2.5 M in hexanes, 104 mmol). The
resultant yellow suspension was stirred at -78°C for 30 min, subsequently
at -45°C for 20 min and cooled down to -78°C again.
(+)-B-methoxydiisopinocamphenyl borane (39.6 g, 125 mmol) in ether (125
mL) was added slowly. After the addition was completed, the mixture was
stirred at -78°C for 1 h and boron trifluoride etherate (18 mL, 142 mmol)
was added dropwisely. Immediately afterwards, a solution of tiglic
aldehyde (7.02 g, 83.5 mmol) in ether (125 mL) was added dropwisely, then
the mixture was kept at -78°C for 3 h. Then 60 mL of saturated NaOAc was
added followed by 30 % H2O2 (60 mL) and further stirred for 30 min and
warmed to room temperature over 12 h. Et2O (100 mL) was added and the
organic layer was collected. The aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3
× 30 mL) and the combined organic layers were then dried over MgSO4.
Removal of the solvent in vacuo and purification by flash chromatography
eluting with a solvent gradient of hexane, then 15% EtOAc/hexane through
20% EtOAc/hexane gave the product (9.83 g, yield 84%, 96/4
diastereoisomer) as a colorless oil. [α]23D = +22° (c 1.14, CH2Cl2); 1H
NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.78 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3 H), 1.51 (s, 3 H), 1.54 (d,
J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H), 2.10 (s, 1 H), 2.15-2.25 (m, 1 H), 3.54 (d, J = 8.7 Hz,
1 H), 5.00-5.10 (m, 2 H), 5.36 (q, J = 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 5.65-5.75 (m, 1 H);
13C NMR (75.4 MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.3, 12.7, 16.4, 41.7, 81.1, 115.6, 122.3,
135.5, 141.2 ppm; IR (film): vmax 3422, 2975, 1452, 1380, 1008, cm-1;
HRMS (CI) m/z for M + H+: 141.1283, calcd. 141.1279.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
