$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (E)-4-Phenyl-3-buten-2-ol (±)-1a5. Method A:
Under a nitrogen atmosphere, to a solution of the carbonyl compound (14
mmol) in THF (70 mL) was dropwise added the corresponding Grignard or
lithium reagents (21 mmol) at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to
warm to room temperature and stirred until the complete consumption of
the substrate. After quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the organic materials
were extracted with EtOAc. The combined organic extract was washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1 or (±)-2,
using trans-cinnamaldehyde (3.00 g, 23 mmol), MeLi (1.6 M in Et2O; 21.0
mL, 34 mmol), and Et2O (75 mL). After 1 h at room temperature, work-up
and column chromatography (hexanes/EtOAc = 5:1 to 5:2).
(E)-4-Phenyl-3-buten-2-ol (±)-1a; (3.30 g, 98%); white solid. mp 30-31
°C. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.38 (d, J= 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.32 (t, J= 8.0
Hz, 2H), 7.24 (t, J= 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.57 (d, J= 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.27 (dd, J=
16.0, 6.5 Hz, 1H), 4.53-4.47 (m, 1H), 1.67 (br s, 1H), 1.38 (d, J= 6.5
Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 136.6, 133.5, 129.4, 128.6, 127.6,
126.4, 68.9, 23.4. IR (CHCl3) ν: 3605, 3017 cm-1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of Optically Active Allyl Esters via Lipase-Vanadium
Combo Catalysis
