$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: b) Methylation. To a solution of scalemic
(17.5 mg, 0.047 mmol, (+)-bisoxazolidine in excess) in anhydrous toluene
was added Me2Zn (2.8 mmol, 1 M in hexanes) at room temperature. After
stirring for 30 minutes, formation of a white precipitate was observed
and benzaldehyde (100 mg, 0.94 mmol) was added at once. Upon completion
of the reaction, the mixture was treated with saturated NH4Cl solution
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried over
anhydrous MgSO4 and removed under reduced pressure. 1-Phenylethanol, was
isolated by flash chromatography (SiO2, 5% EtOAc in hexanes).
Chromatographic purification (hexanes:ethyl acetate = 95:5) gave
1-Phenylethanol as a colorless oil, yield 92% (106 mg, 0.86 mmol), 88%
ee. Chromatographic purification (hexanes:ethyl acetate = 85:15) gave
4-Phenyl-but-3-en-2-ol as colorless oil, yield 94% (115 mg, 0.88 mmol),
41% ee. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 1.33 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3H), 2.81 (bs,
1H), 4.42 (m, 1H), 6.20 (dd, J = 6.3 Hz, 15.1 Hz, 1H), 6.53 (d, J = 15.1
Hz, 1H), 7.18-7.36 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 24.0, 69.4,
127.0, 128.4, 129.1, 129.8, 134.2, 137.3. The ee was determined by HPLC
on Chiralcel OD, hexanes:2-propanol = 85:15, t1 = 7.8 min, t2 = 10.5 min,
α = 1.47.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 41% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chiral Amplification Based on Enantioselective Dual-Phase Distribution of
a Scalemic Bisoxazolidine Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Shuanglong; Wolf, Christian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(16), 2965-2968

