$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(1S,2R)-(+)-1-Cyclohexyl-2-methyl-4-triisopropylsilyl-3-butyn- 1-ol (7a).
Standard Procedure for Allenylzinc Additions. A flame-dried 50 mL flask
was charged with THF (13 mL) and Pd(OAc)2 (15.2 mg, 0.07 mmol, 5 mol %).
Upon complete dissolution of the Pd(OAc)2, the mixture was cooled to -78
°C, and PPh3 (17.7 mg, 0.07 mmol, 5 mol %) was added. When the mixture
became homogeneous, TIPS mesylate (S)-1c (490 mg, 1.61 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
and cyclohexanecarboxaldehyde (160 ímL, 1.32 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were added,
and then Et2Zn (1 M in hexanes, 4.0 mL, 4.0 mmol, 3 equiv) was added
dropwise over 5 min. The resulting yellow solution was warmed to -20 °C
and stirred for 14 h. The reaction was quenched by pouring over a rapidly
stirring solution of saturated aqueous NH4Cl (25 mL), and after 15 min,
the phases were separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O.
The combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography (hexanes to 10% EtOAc/hexanes) to yield alcohol 7a (363
mg, 85% yield of the anti diastereomer and 17 mg, 4% yield of the syn
diastereomer) as a clear oil:
(3R,4S)-(+)-3-Methyl-l-trimethylsilyl-l-decyn-5-en-4-ol (22b). The
standard procedure for allenylzinc addition was employed with THF (13
mL), Pd(OAc)2 (14.9 mg, 0.07 mmol), PPh3 (17.4 mg, 0.07 mmol),
TIPSmesylate (S)-lc (486 mg, 1.6 mmol), trans-2-heptenal (150 mg, 1.3
mmol) and Et2Zn (1M in hexanes, 4 mL, 4 mmol) affording alcohol 22b (52
mg, 12% yield, 80:20 mixture of anti and syn diastereomers separable by
flash chromatography with 20% EtaO/hexanes elutant plus 146 mg, 77% yield
of the 1,4-ethyl addition product 23) as a clear oil: [α]20 D = +13.7 (c
0.85, CHCl3); IR (film) 3408, 2942, 2865, 2162, 1464 cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 5.69-5.78 (m, 1H), 5.44-5.52 (m, 1H), 3.86-3.91 (m, 1H),
2.55-2.64 (m, 1H), 2.09 (s, 1H), 2.05 (q, J = 2.05 Hz, 2H), 1.26-1.40 (m,
4H), 1.19 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.06 (s, 21H), 0.89 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H);
13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 134.2, 130.1, 109.7, 83.6, 75.9, 35.1, 32.2, 31.4,
22.4, 18.8, 17.5, 14.1, 11.4.
