$DATUM Aldehyde 13. To a solution of aldehyde 12 (5.69 g, 20.3 mmol, 1.0 eq) in
tetrahydrofurane (200 mL, degased by freeze-pump-thaw method) was
successively added vinyltributylstannane (6.50 mL, 7.05 g, 22.3 mmol, 1.1
eq), triphenylphosphine (1.07 g, 4.06 mmol, 0.2 eq), and
tris(dibenzylidenaceton) dipalladium (1.86 g, 2.03 mmol, 0.1 eq) at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was warmed to 50 °C and stirred for 16
h. Water (200 mL) and diethyl ether (200 mL) were added and the aqueous
layer was extracted with diethyl ether (3x100 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with brine (100 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
the solvent removed in vacuo (product is volatile! 30 °C, 300 mbar) was
obtained by repeated column chromatography (20 - 40% Et2O/PE). Aldehyde
13 as a yellow oil, yield 3.51 g, 19.5 mmol, 96%. [α]20D = +12.5 (c =
1.0, CHCl3); Rf = 0.38 (30% EtOAc/PE); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 9.41
(s, 1H), 6.63 - 6.50 (m, 2H), 6.11 (ddd, J = 10.9, 1.2, 0.8 Hz, 1H), 5.25
(dd, J = 16.8, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 5.16 (dd, J = 10.2, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 4.27 (t, J =
6.5 Hz, 1H), 2.71 - 2.56 (m, 2H), 1.80 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 3H), 1.76 (d, J =
1.2 Hz, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 195.2, 150.1, 141.0, 139.2,
132.3, 126.7, 118.4, 76.0, 34.7, 12.5, 9.6 ppm; ESI-HRMS: C11H16O2Na
[M+Na]+ calculated: 203.1048, found: 203.1014.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille reaction
