$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Addition of Et2Zn to
aldehyde To a solution of chiral ligand 3d (10.6 mg, 0.03 mmol) in
toluene (10 ml) at room temperature was added dropwise a solution of
diethylzinc (1.0 M solution in hexane, 2 ml, 2 mmol). The resulting
solution was stirred at room temperature for 15 min. Aldehyde (1 mmol)
was added in one portion at 0°C and the reaction mixture was stirred for
24h at room temperature. The reaction was quenched by the addition of 1M
HCl solution (30 ml) and the mixture was extRacted with ethyl acetate (30
ml x 2). The combined organic extRacts were washed with brine (30 ml x
2), dried (MgSO4), and concentRated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
flash column chromatography on silica gel with ethyl acetate/hexanes
(1:7) to give the pure alcohol product. 1-Phenyl-1-propanol
(E)-1-Phenyl-1-penten-3-ol yeild 95%. [α]D25 = +7.14 (c = 5.0, CHCl3)
{lit.2 [α]D22 = -5.7 (c = 100, CHCl3) for 96% ee (S)}; 86% ee by HPLC
analysis (Chiralcel OD column, hexane:2-propanol = 95:5, 1 ml/min, 254 nm
UV detector), tR = 9.63 min for (R) and tR = 14.68 min for (S).
