$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. Diethylzinc addition to benzaldehyde 3.1
General procedure for the base-catalysed diethylzinc addition to
aldehydes Method A A toluene solution (2.5 mL) of ligand (0.05 mmol) was
prepared. After stirring the solution for 5 min at ambient temperature,
diethylzinc (2 mL, 1 M solution in hexane, 2 mmol) was added and stirred
for an additional 30 min. The resulting solution was cooled to 0 °C and
benzaldehyde (1 mmol) was added. The reaction was stirred for 48 h at 0
°C. Quenching with 5% HCl (5 mL) followed by extraction with diethyl
ether (2 x 5 mL), drying over magnesium sulphate and column
chromatographic separation using silica gel (5:1 pentane/EtOAc) gave
1-phenylpropanol. (E)-1-Phenyl-1-penten-3-ol The crude product was
obtained from trans-cinnamaldehyde benzaldehyde according to the general
procedure outlined above. Purification by flash column chromatography
(5:1 pentane/EtOAc) furnished pure (E)-1-phenyl-1-penten-3-ol as an oily
residue Yield 99%. • 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.79 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H,
CH2CH3), 1.57-1.45 (m, 2H, CH2CH3), 1.83 (s, 1H, OH), 3.84-4.46 (m, 1H,
CHOH), 5.98 (dd, J = 16.0, 6.8 Hz, 1H, Holefin), 6.40 (d, J = 16 Hz, 1H,
Holefin), 7.09-7.24 (m, 5H, Har) • HPLC separation conditions: Chiracel®
OD column, 256nm UV detector, 90:10 hexane/2-propanol, 1.0 mL/min; tR =
7.8 min for (R), tR = 11.6 min for (S).
