$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Asymmetric Ethylation of 1-Naphthaldehyde
Catalyzed by BINOL Derivative 2f (A Representative Procedure; Table 3,
entry 7). To a solution of 2f (5.1 mg, 0.01 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (8 mL) at
room temperature under argon atmosphere was added titanium
tetraisopropoxide (0.413 mL, 1.4 mmol). The resulting solution was
stirred for 10 min at room temperature. To this at 0 °C was added
diethylzinc (1M in hexane, 3 mL, 3.0 mmol) and stirring was continued for
10 min. To the resulting mixture was added 1-naphthaldehyde (0.156 g, 1.0
mmol) at 0 °C. After being stirred for 2 h, the reaction mixture was
quenched by the addition of aqueous 1N HCl and extracted twice with ethyl
acetate. The organic layers were washed with aqueous 5% NaHCO3, dried
(Na2SO4), and concentrated in vacuo. Kugelrohr distillation of the
residue at reduced pressure (160 ºC, 2 mm Hg) afforded 0.177 g (95%
yield) of (R)-1-(1-naphthyl)-1-propanol (95% ee). The ee values was
determined by HPLC analysis using a Chiralcel OD column (0.8 mL/min, 10%
i-PrOH in hexane); retention times: 11.0 min (minor S-enantiomer) and
19.0 min (major R-enantiomer). The absolute structure of the product was
determined by comparing the retention time with that of an authentic
sample prepared by asymmetric ethylation using (R)-BINOL as a ligand.7
(E)-1-Phenylpent-1-en-3-ol (Table 3, entry 12) (Chiralcel OD column, 1.0
mL/min, 3% i-PrOH in hexane); retention times: 18.5 min (major
R-enantiomer) and 32.3 min (minor S-enantiomer).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, ee 92%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
