$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: B. Et2Zn addition to aldehydes To a solution
of 4 (5 mol%) in THF at 0°C was added neat Et2Zn (2 equiv) and the
mixture was stirred for 10 min. The aldehyde was added and the reaction
mixture stirred for 2 h at 0°C. Saturatated NH4Cl (aq) solution was added
dropwise, the reaction mixture was partitioned between EtOAc-H2O, and the
aqueous layer was extraced with EtOAc (2 x). The organic layer was washed
with H2O (1 x), brine (1), and dried over Na2SO4. An aliquot of undecane
was added to the solution, which was then analyzed by GC equipped with
β-cyclodextrin column. Assay yields were determined on a Hewlett Packard
6840 GC equipped with a -cyclodextrin capillary column (30 m x 0.25 mm
I.D., 0.25 mM) using undecane as an external standard and the oven
temperature was 90° isotherm. 1-Phenyl-1-penten-3 - o l 4,5 This compound
was prepared according to general method B. The enantiomeric excess was
determined by GC (column: β-cyclodextrin, 90°C isotherm). 1H NMR (300
MHz) δ 7.40-7.18 (m, 5H), 6.55 (d, 1H, J = 15.8 Hz), 6.09 (dd, 1H, J =
15.8, 6.8 Hz), 4.19-4.15 (m, 1H), 1.85 (br s), 1.66-1.63 (m, 2H), 0.94
(t, 3H, J = 7.5 Hz) ppm; 13C NMR (75.5 MHz) δ 136.7, 132.2, 130.3, 128.5,
127.4, 126.3, 74.3, 30.1, 10.1 ppm.
