$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: a) Ethylation. To a solution of scalemic (7.0
mg, 0.019 mmol, (+)-bisoxazolidine in excess) in anhydrous toluene was
added Et2Zn (2.8 mmol, 1 M in hexanes) at room temperature. After
stirring for 30 minutes, formation of a white precipitate was observed
and benzaldehyde, benzaldehyde (100 mg, 0.94 mmol) was added at once.
Upon completion of the reaction, the mixture was treated with saturated
NH4Cl solution and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers
were dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and removed under reduced pressure,
followed by flash chromatography (SiO2, 5% EtOAc in hexanes), and
chromatographic purification (hexanes:ethyl acetate = 95: 5).
Chromatographic purification (hexanes:ethyl acetate = 85:15) gave
1-Phenyl-pent-1-en-3-ol as colorless oil, yield 97% (148 mg, 0.91
mmol),40% ee. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 0.94 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H),
1.52-1.65 (m, 2H), 2.28 (bs, 1H), 4.16 (m, 1H), 6.18 (dd, J = 6.8 Hz,
16.4 Hz, 1H), 6.53 (d, J = 16.4 Hz, 1H), 7.18-7.36 (m, 5H). 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ = 10.4, 30.8, 74.9, 127.0, 128.1, 129.1, 130.9, 132.9,
137.4. The ee was determined by HPLC on Chiralcel OD, hexanes:2-propanol
= 85:15, t1 = 11.2 min, t2 = 14.9 min, α = 1.40.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 40% ee
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chiral Amplification Based on Enantioselective Dual-Phase Distribution of
a Scalemic Bisoxazolidine Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liu, Shuanglong; Wolf, Christian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2007), 9(16), 2965-2968

