$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for enantioselectivity
addition of diethylzinc to aldehydes in the presence of Ti-4 catalyst A
suspension of the polymer-supported 4 (50 mg, 0.38 mmol/g) in DCM was
allowed to stirred under Ar at room temperature for 12 h to swell the
polymer. Ti(OiPr)4 (60 μL, 0.175 mmol) was added and the mixture became
red immediately. After 10 min, a solution of diethylzinc (0.38 mL of 1M
solution in DCM, 0.38 mmol) was introduced to the above reaction. The
mixture was further stirred for 20 min. Benzaldehyde (13 μL, 0.1 mmol)
was added dropwise at 0 °C and the reaction was allowed to proceed for a
period of time at the end of which cool solution of NH4Cl was introduced
to quench the reaction. The polymer was removed by filtration. The
alcohol was isolated to give colorless oil by column chromatography
(silica gel) after extraction with an organic solvent and the ee value
was determined by HPLC with Daicel Chiracel OD column. It was difficult
to determine the ee values of the aliphatic alcohols, so the alcohols
were transferred into their benzoate derivatives by the reaction of
benzoyl chloride and the alcohols in common method and then were analyzed
by HPLC with chiral column.General procedure for the benzoyl derivatives
of the alcohols To a solution of the resulting alcohols (0.5 mmol) in DCM
(0.5 mL) was added dropwise benzoyl chloride (1 mmol) at 0°C . After the
completion measured by TLC a solution of 10 % NaOH was introduced to
quench the reaction. The organic phase was washed respectively with 10%
Na2CO3, H2O and brine, and dried over anhydrous Na2SO4. The crude product
was purified by column chromatography on silica gel (ethyl acetate:
petroleum ether) to give the benzoyl derivatives. 1-phenyl-1-penten-3-ol,
yield (97%) 1H NMR (CDCl3, 80M) δ 0.99 (t, J=7.4 Hz, 3H), 1.36-1.88 (m,
3H, OH, CH2), 4.27 (m, 1H), 6.15, 6.35 (dd, J=5.9 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (d, J=
15.9 Hz, 1H), 7.36 (m, 5H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, polymer-bound ligand gave higher selectivity than
corresponding unbound Ti-BINOL complex
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Polymer-Supported BINOL Ligand for the Titanium-Catalyzed Diethylzinc
Addition to Aldehydes: A Remarkable Positive Influence of the Support on
the Enantioselectivity of the Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yang, Xiao-Wu; Sheng, Jian-Heng; Da, Chao-Shan; Wang, Heng-Shan; Su, Wu;
Wang, Rui; Chan, Albert S. C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(2), 295-296

