$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Navenone B. To a solution of cinnamaldehyde (1.078 g, 8.0
mmol, 98% purity) in THF (25 mL) was added vinylmagnesium bromide (1.0 M
in THF, 9.6 mL, 9.6 mmol) dropwise at 0 °C. The reaction mixture was
stirred at 0 °C for 30 min. Then the reaction mixture was allowed to warm
to room temperature and further stirred at room temperature for 2 h.
Diluted aqueous NH4Cl solution was added to quench the reaction, and the
reaction mixture was extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL). The combined
organic layers were washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, filtered and
evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel
column chromatography (EtOAc/hexanes = 1:10) to afford the desired
product. Product; 1s. Yield: (1.237 g, 96%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.41-7.35 (m, 2H), 7.34-7.28 (m, 2H), 7.27-7.21 (m, 1H), 6.61 (d, J =
15.6 Hz, 1H), 6.23 (dd, J = 16.0, 6.4 Hz, 1H), 5.97 (ddd, J = 17.2, 10.4,
6.0 Hz, 1H), 5.34 (dt, J = 17.2, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 5.19 (d, J = 10.4, 1.2 Hz,
1H), 4.81 (br s, 1H), 1.89 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 139.2,
136.5, 130.8, 130.3, 128.5, 127.7, 126.5, 115.4, 73.8.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM dropwise addition of vinylMgBr/THF (stage 1), Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 1,n-Rearrangement of Allylic Alcohols Promoted by Hot Water: Application
to the Synthesis of Navenone B, a Polyene Natural Product
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Li, Pei-Fang; Wang, Heng-Lu; Qu, Jin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(9), 3955-3962

