$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Grignard Reactions in
RTIL 2-Isopropyl-1,3-dimethylimidazolium Triflimide. To a stirred
solution of 68 mg (0.50 mmol) of p-anisaldehyde in RTIL
2-Isopropyl-1,3-dimethylimidazolium Triflimide was added 183 μL (0.55
mmol) of a 3.0 M solution of methyl magnesium chloride in THF. The
reaction vessel was sealed and stirred for 2 h. The reaction was then
quenched by the addition of 2 mL of 0.2 M hydrochloric acid and extracted
with 10% ether in hexanes (4 x 3 mL). The combined organic extracts were
dried with magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo. The
crude residue was purified on silica (50% ether/hexanes as eluent) to
afford desired product. Yield 94%. Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Grignard Reactions in Imidazolium Ionic Liquids
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Handy, Scott T.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(12), 4659-4662

