$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (3S,4S,5E,7S,9R)-Tetramethyl-1,5-undecadien-4-ol (11). Following the
literature procedure, trans-2-Butene (0.28 g, 0.52 mL, 5.0 mmol) was
condensed in a flame-dried graduate cylinder at -78 °C and added to a
solution of KOt-Bu (2.7 mL, 1 M in THF, 2.7 mmol) at -78 °C. n-Buli (1.1
mL, 2.5 M in hexane, 2.7 mmol) was added slowly to the mixture while
maintaining the temperature at -78 °C. The yellow mixture was warmed to
-45 °C for 30 min, recooled to -78 °C, and a solution of dry
(-)-(Ipc)2BOMe (0.84 g, 2.7 mmol) was added via cannula. After stirring
at -78 °C for 30 min, the viscous yellow mixture had totally dissolved.
BF3.Et2O (0.51 g, 0.45 mL, 3.6 mmol) was added slowly, and the solution
was stirred at -78 °C until a white cloudy suspension formed. To this
mixture was added (4S, 6R)-2,4,6-trimethyl-2-octenal (0.34 g, 2.0 mmol)
in 0.8 mL of THF via cannula. The mixture was stirred at -78 °C over 10
h, quenched at -78 °C with 2 M NaOH solution (1.3 mL) and 30% H2O2
solution (1.7 mL), and warmed to 23 °C with stirring under Ar for 20 h.
The aqueous layer was separated and extracted with EtOAc. The combined
organic extracts were washed successively with Na2SO3 solution and brine,
dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The crude mixture was
purified by flash chromatography in hexane followed by 5% EtOAc/hexane to
afford 383 mg of the desired product in 85% yield (anti/syn = 10/1 =
91/9). [α]D = + 2 ° (c 1.6, CHCl3); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.75-0.9 (m, 9 H),
0.95-1.1 (m, 3 H), 1.1-1.4 (m, 5 H), 1.59 (s, 3 H), 1.70 (s, 1 H),
2.2-2.35 (m, 1 H), 2.4-2.55 (m, 1 H), 3.58 (d, J=8.9 Hz, 1 H), 5.05-5.2
(m, 3 H), 5.65-5.8 (m, 1 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 10.79, 11.19, 16.81,
19.56, 20.82, 28.96, 29.60, 31.99, 42.20, 44.79, 81.68, 116.31, 132.65,
136.35, 141.51; IR (neat) 3446, 2960, 2926, 1717, 1668, 1638, 1456, 1377
cm-1; LRMS (EI) calcd. for C15H28O M+ 224, found 224.
