$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 1l was prepared via a three-step sequence as outlined below: To
a 50 mL round-bottomed flask was added THF (30 mL) and phenyl lithium (16
mL, ca. 1.8 M in dibutylether). The dark red solution was cooled down to
-78 °C and trans-crotonaldehyde (1.3 mL, 15.7 mmol) was added drop-wise
over 5 minutes, causing the red color to become browner. After stirring
for 25 min. at -78 °C the reaction mixture was warmed up to room
temperature. After stirring 30 min. at room temperature the reaction was
quenched by drop-wise addition of saturated ammonium chloride solution
(17 mL) followed by distilled water (5 mL). The organic phase was
separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with diethyl ether (3 × 25
mL). The combined organic components extracted with brine (20 mL) and
dried with anhydrous sodium sulfate. Gravity filtration followed by
concentration in vacuo afforded a yellow solution that was flushed
through a pad of silica gel using gradient elution of 100% hexanes to
100% diethyl ether. Concentration of the fractions obtained from flushing
with diethyl ether in vacuo afforded dark yellow oil in 91% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
