$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-1-Phenyl-2-buten-1-ol (±)-2a. Method A: Under a nitrogen atmosphere,
to a solution of the carbonyl compound (14 mmol) in THF (70 mL) was
dropwise added the corresponding Grignard or lithium reagents (21 mmol)
at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature
and stirred until the complete consumption of the substrate. After
quenching with sat. aq. NH4Cl, the organic materials were extracted with
EtOAc. The combined organic extract was washed with brine, dried over
MgSO4, and evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel) to give (±)-1 or (±)-2, using crotonaldehyde
(500 mg, 7.0 mmol), PhMgBr (1.0 M in THF; 10.5 mL, 11 mmol), and THF (20
mL). After 1 h at room temperature, work-up and column chromatography
(hexanes/EtOAc = 10:1) gave (±)-2a (936 mg, 90%) as a colorless oil. 1H
NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.40-7.25 (m, 5H), 5.78 (dq, J= 15.5, 6.5 Hz,
1H), 5.70 (ddd, J= 15.5, 7.0, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 5.17 (dd, J= 7.0, 3.5 Hz, 1H),
1.85 (d, J= 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.73 (d, J= 6.5 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ: 143.3, 133.5, 128.4, 127.52, 127.50, 126.1, 75.2, 17.7. IR
(CHCl3) ν: 3601, 3017 cm-1.
