$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Phenyl-hept-1-en-3-ol (7a): To 1.90 mL (2.00 g, 15.1 mmol) of
cinnamaldehyde in 15 mL of Et2O at -78°C was added 10.4 mL (16.6 mmol) of
n-butyl lithium in hexanes (1.6 M) via syringe. The mixture was stirred
at -78 °C for 30 min, then quenched carefully with sat. aq. NH4Cl. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (3x), the combined organic layers
were dried over Na2SO4, filtered and the crude product mixture was
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography on SiO2
(7.5:1 hexanes/EtOAc), to give as a yellow oil 1-Phenyl-hept-1-en-3-ol,
yield 2.57 g, 89%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.46-7.22 (m, 5H), 6.58 (d,
J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 6.23 (dd, J = 15.9, 6.8 Hz, 1H), 4.29 (q, J = 6.5 Hz,
1H), 1.69-1.50 (m, 2H), 1.49-1.30 (m, 4H), 0.93 (t, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
