$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General Procedure (B) for the formation of
allylic alcohols: Benzaldehyde or ketone derivatives were diluted in dry
THF (6 mL). The grignard reagent was added slowly at 0°C. The mixture was
stirred 30 min and allowed to warm to RT. The reaction was monitored by
TLC. Following full consumption of the substrate, the mixture was
quenched with a saturated solution of NH4Cl (10 mL) and extracted with
ether (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic phase was dried over anhydrous
MgSO4. Removal of the solvent under reduced pressure followed by flash
column chromatography (Silica, Eluent: Hexane/AcOEt4/1) afforded the
alcohol derivatives. 4-(1-hydroxyallyl)benzonitrile:3
3-methyl-1-phenylbut-2-en-1-ol:6 Following the procedure B with
benzaldehyde (0.6 mL, 5.64 mmol), 2-methyl-1-propenylmagnesium bromide0.5
M (15 mL, 7.5 mmol) gave the compound (782 mg, 86%) as a pale yellow
liquid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,CDCl3) δ 7.33-7.40 (m, 4H, Ar-H), 7.24-7.28 (m,
1H, Ar-H), 5.40 -5.49 (m, 2H, CH-OH, CH-CHOH), 1.81 (s,3H, CH3), 1.76 (s,
3H, CH3); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.2, 135.4, 128.5 (2C), 127.7,
127.3, 125.8 (2C), 70.8, 25.9, 18.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Formation of Allylic Chlorides from Carbonyl Derivatives
