$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound allylic alcohol. To a solution of iodide (1.21 g, 3.88 mmol) in
20 mL THF was addedt -BuLi (8.5 mL of a 1.7 M solution in pentane, 14.5
mmol) at -78 °C and the mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 10 min. Then
acetaldehyde (260 μl, 4.6 mmol) was added to themixture and the mixture
was stirred at -78 °C for 30 min. The mixture was quenched by the
addition of H2O and extracted with EtOAc. The extract was dried (NaSO4),
filtered,and evaporated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(1 : 1 hexanes/EtOAc) to afford the alcohol yield 750 mg, 84%. FT-IR
νmax(neat, cm-1) 3371, 2929, 2857, 1666, 1472, 1463, 1377.1H NMRδH (400
MHz; CDCl3) 5.41 (1 H, dd, J 6.9 and 6.1), 4.69 (1 H, q, J 6.5), 4.27 (1
H, dd, J 14.3 and 6.9), 4.13 (1 H, dd, J 14.3 and 6.9), 1.87 (1 H, brs),
1.73 (3 H, s), 1.25 (3 H, d, J 6.5), 0.89 (9 H, s) and 0.08 (6 H, s).13C
NMR δC (100 MHz; CDCl3) 141.8, 125.9, 66.3, 59.2, 26.3, 21.5, 18.7, 18.2
and_4.8.FABHRMS m/z 231.1787 (M+ + H). C12H27O2Si requires 231.1780.
