$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the enantioselective
propargylation with 1c-Cr complex. (R)-1-phenylbut-3-yn-1-ol (2) A
mixture of 1c (34.0 mg, 0.0597 mmol) and CrCl2 (6.2 mg, 0.050 mmol) was
azeotroped with toluene and dried under high vacuum, and was dissolved in
THF (2 ml) under Ar atmosphere. The color turned to deep brown gradually.
After stirring at 60°C for 12h, to the mixture was added DIPEA (0.026 ml,
0.15 mmol). After stirring at 60°C for additional 1h, H2O (0.1 ml) was
added in open air. The mixture was filtered through Celite, and
evaporated in vacuo. To the residue was added H2O (15 ml) and CH2Cl2 (15
ml), and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (15 ml × 3). The
combined organic layer was washed with brine (20 ml), dried over MgSO4,
evaporated. A mixture of the crude complex and Mn (56.7 mg, 1.03 mmol)
was azeotroped with toluene, and was suspended in DME (2 ml). After
stirring 15 min, to the suspension were added DIPEA (0.026 ml, 0.15 mmol)
and propargylbromide (0.075 ml, 1.0 mmol). After 5 min, to the mixture
was added benzaldehyde (0.050 ml, 0.49 mmol), TMSCl (0.125 ml, 0.98 mmol)
successively, and the resulting mixture was stirred for 12h at room
temperature. The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (0.5
ml), filtered through Celite, and evaporated. The crude product was
dissolved in THF (2 ml), and the stirred mixture was treated with TBAF
(1.0 ml, 1 M solution). The reaction was quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl (2 ml), extracted with Et2O (10 ml × 4), dried over Na2SO4, and
evaporated. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(hexane/ethyl acetate=8/1). (R)-(E)-1-phenylhex-1-en-5-yn-3-ol (4), 16
hours, yield 91%. [α]D24 -11.1 (c 1.50, benzene), (lit.15h[α]D24 -59.27
(c 1.35, benzene)); ee was determined by HPLC; Daicel Chiral Pack OD-H
0.46 cm ϕ × 25 cm; hexane/isopropanol=19/1; flow rate=0.5 ml/min);
retention time: 33.7 min.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
