$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Coupling procedure with the Cr-catalyst
derived from sulfonamide D To a vial charged with a stir bar were added
ligand D (8.8 mg, 0.022 mmol), CrBr3 (5.8 mg, 0.020 mmol), Mn (33 mg,
0.60 mmol), THF (distilled from LiAlH4, 1 mL), and Et3N (3.1 μL 0.022
mmol) in a glove box. After tightly capped with a septum, the vial was
moved out from the glove box and the mixture was stirred at 42 °C for 1.5
h. The vial was placed into the glove box and the serum cap was removed.
After addition of 2,6- lutidine (2.8 μL, 0.024 mmol), the mixture was
stirred for 15 min at rt. Then, without stirring, propargyl bromide
(80wt% in toluene, 68 mg, 0.46 mmol), the aldehyde (0.20 mmol), and
Zr(Cp)2Cl2 (70 mg, 0.24 mmol) were successively introduced into the
mixture. Once again, after tightly capped with a septum, the vial was
moved out from the glove box and placed in a 0 °C bath and stirred for 15
h. The mixture was then diluted with ethyl acetate, filtered through a
silica gel pad, washed with NaHCO3 (20 mL) and extracted with ethyl
acetate (20 mL, 3 times). The organic layer was washed with brine, dried
over MgSO4, and concentrated to give the crude product which was purified
by flash column chromatography (20:1 → 5:1 hexanes/EtOAc) to give the
product. The enantiomeric excess was determined from 1H NMR analysis of
its (+)-Mosher ester. Coupling with the Cr-catalyst derived from (R)-D:
89% and 70% ee (page S-41).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, in-situ generated catalyst (stage 1), recyclable ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Enantioselective Cr-Mediated Propargylation: Application to
Halichondrin Synthesis
