$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,E)-1-Cyclohexylbut-2-en-1-ol (ent-6). To the lithium powder (1.19 g,
169.3 mmol) under argon was added dry ether (20 mL) and the suspension
was cooled to –35 ºC. With stirring, a solution of (E)-1-bromo-propene
(10.0 g, 82.6 mmol, in 40 mL ether) was added dropwise. The mixture was
stirred at -35ºC for 2 h and treated dropwise with zinc bromide solution
(19.5 g, 86.7 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for an additional 1
h at 0 ºC and then a solution of lithium (-)-N-methylephedrate, prepared
by the addition of n-butyllithium (2.5 M in hexanes, 34.7 mL, 86.1 mmol)
to a solution of (-)-Nmethylephedrine (15.6 g, 86.7 mmol) in toluene (20
mL) at 0 ºC, was added by cannula. The solution was stirred for 1 h at 0
ºC and cyclohexanecarboxaldehyde (7.42 g, 66.1 mmol) was added neat.
After stirring for 1 h at 0 ºC, the reaction was quenched by the addition
of saturated aqueous ammonium chloride solution. The organic phase was
separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with ether (3 x 50 mL). The
organic phases were combined, washed with a second portion of the
ammonium chloride solution, dried (MgSO4), and concentrated.
Chromatography (HE: EA = 10: 1) gave alcohol ent-6(8.56 g, 84%, 92% ee.
according to NMR study of Mosher ester) as clear liquid.
(-)-Nmethylephedrine was recovered quantitatively from the aqueous phases
by basification to pH= 12 with 2 N NaOH solution and extraction into
ether. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 5.78-5.66 (dqd, J = 15.2, 6.4, 0.8 Hz,
1H), 5.51-5.44 (ddq, J = 15.2, 7.6, 1.6 Hz, 1H), 3.78- 3.73 (td, J = 7.2,
2.8 Hz, 1H), 1.87-1.83 (m, 1H), 1.77-1.63 (m, 8H), 1.42-0.85 (m, 6H), IR
(neat) νmax 3391 (br), 2929, 2853, 1650, 1448, 1002, 967; HRMS (EI) m/z
cacld for C10H18O (M+) 154.1358, found: 154.1358.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, in-situ generated reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Asymmetric Catalysis Route to anti,anti Stereotriads, Illustrated by
Applications
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Parker, Kathlyn A.; Xie, Qiuzhe
