$DATUM 7-Methyl-5-(phenylseleno)oct-2-en-4-ol : BuLi (1.6 M in hexane, 0.11 mL,
0.18 mmol) was added dropwise to a stirred and cooled (-78 °C) solution
of stannane (46 mg, 0.09 mmol) in THF (3 mL) (Ar atmosphere). Stirring
was continued for 15 min at -78 °C, and a solution of crotonaldehyde (19
mg, 0.27 mmol) in THF (1mL) was added dropwise (ca 1 min). Stirring was
continued for 30 min and the mixture was quenched with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl. The cooling bath was removed and stirring was continued for 30
min. The aqueous phase was extracted with EtOAc and the combined organic
extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated. Flash chromatography of the
residue over silicagel (1.0 x 20 cm), using 0-10% EtOAc-hexane, gave
7-Methyl-5-(phenylseleno)oct-2-en-4-ol, pale yellow oil, yield 19.4 mg,
73%. FTIR (microscope) 3443, 3071, 3057, 2956, 2868 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3,
300 MHz) (1:1 mixture of stereoisomers) δ 0.85 (dd, J = 6.6, 4.2 Hz, 3
H), 0.92 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.36-1.44 (m, 1 H), 1.49-1.58 (m, 1 H),
1.66-1.73 (m, 3 H), 1.83-2.13 (m, 1 H), 2.44 (d, J = 5.1 Hz, 0.5 H), 2.76
(s, 0.5 H), 3.05-3.18 (m, 0.5 H), 3.32-3.43 (m, 0.5 H), 3.88 (t, J = 6.9
Hz, 0.5 H), 4.12 (s, 0.5 H), 5.40-5.54 (m, 1 H), 5.62-5.78 (m, 1 H),
7.22-7.34 (m, 3 H), 7.54-7.64 (m, 2 H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ 17.7
(q), 17.8 (q), 21.4 (q), 21.6 (q), 23.2 (q), 23.3 (q), 26.2 (d), 26.2
(d), 40.2 (t), 40.5 (t), 53.9 (d), 54.4 (d), 73.7 (d), 74.4 (d), 127.5
(d), 127.6 (s), 127.9 (d), 128.5 (d),129.0 (d), 129.1 (d), 129.3 (d),
129.5 (s), 130.4 (d), 131.2 (d), 134.5 (d), 135.5 (d); exact mass m/z
calcd for C15H55O80Se 298.08359, found 298.08406.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM isomer mix.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
