$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Grignard Reaction: Allylic Alcohol (±)-6d. Magnesium powder (24.31 g/mol,
123 mg, 5.06 mmol, 1.5 equiv) was placed in a two neck round bottom flask
und covered with Et2O. The formation of the Grignard reagent was
initiated by adding approximately one tenth of the
(chloromethyl)trimethylsilane (C4H11ClSi, 122.67 g/mol, 0.879 g/mL, 615
mg, 0.70 mL, 5.01 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and one drop of bromine. After the
reaction mixture turned cloudy and started to reflux, a solution of the
remaining silane in Et2O (3.5 mL) was added carefully. After the addition
of the silane was completed, the greyish reaction mixture was gently
refluxed for 2 h and then cooled to room temperature. A solution of the
aldehyde S6 (225.15 g/mol, 760 mg, 3.38 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was dissolved in
Et2O (1.8 mL) and added dropwise. After being stirred for 2.5 h at room
temperature, the greyish suspension was diluted by careful addition of
saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution at 0 °C. The layers were separated and
the aqueous phase was extracted with Et2O (3×). The combined organic
phases were dried (MgSO4) and the solvent was evaporated at reduced
pressure. Purification of the residue by chromatography
(cyclohexane/ethyl acetate 250/1 to 20/1) delivered the compound. Yield:
(313.37 g/mol, 960 mg, 3.06 mmol, 91%), pale yellow oil. The double bond
configuration was deduced from 3J(1H, 1H) coupling constant analysis of
the signals at 5.43 ppm (15.2 Hz) and 5.74 ppm (15.2 Hz). Rf 0.34
(cyclohexane/ethyl acetate 5/1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 0.02 (s, 9H),
0.91 (dd, J1 = 14.3 Hz, J2 = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 0.93 (dd, J1 = 14.3 Hz, J2 =
7.3 Hz, 1H), 1.21 (br s, 1H), 3.51 (dt, J1 = 7.7 Hz, J2 = 1.3 Hz, 2H),
4.20 (q, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 5.43 (ddt, J1 = 15.2 Hz, J2 = 7.1 Hz, J3 = 1.0
Hz, 1H), 5.74 (dtd, J1 = 15.2 Hz, J2 = 7.5 Hz, J3 = 1.1 Hz, 1H),
7.26-7.31 (m, 3H), 7.50-7.53 (m, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ -0.6,
26.4, 29.4, 70.7, 126.0, 127.5, 129.1, 129.8, 134.0, 138.1; IR ν 3425
(s), 3065 (m), 2955 (s), 2900 (s), 1645 (w), 1475 (m), 1425 (m), 1300
(m), 1250 (s), 1190 (m), 1035 (m), 965 (m), 850 (s); Anal. Calcd. for
C14H22OSeSi: C, 53.7; H, 7.1; Found: C, 53.9; H, 7.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Grignard reaction, incremental addition (silane, stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
