$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ni/Cr-Mediated Coupling To a solution of 8a
(6.2 mg, 0.021 mmol) and proton sponge (4.5 mg, 0.021 mmol) in CH3CN (1.0
mL) was added CrCl2 (2.5 mg, 0.020 mmol) under nitrogen. The mixture was
stirred for 1.0 h at room temperature. To the mixture was added LiCl (17
mg, 0.40 mmol), Mn (22 mg, 0.40 mmol), NiCl2(dppp) (ca. 1~2 mg, ca. 0.002
~ 0.004 mmol), 2-iodo-1-hexene 2a (84 mg, 0.40 mmol), hydrocinnamaldehyde
1 (27 μL, 0.20 mmol), and bis(cyclopentadienyl)zirconium dichloride (58
mg, 0.20 mmol) successively. The mixture was stirred for 12 h at room
temperature under nitrogen and diluted with ethyl acetate. To the mixture
was added Florisil (ca. 100 mg). The mixture was stirred for 30 min.,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (elution with
hexane/ethyl acetate = 19 : 1 to 9 : 1) to give 2-butyl-5-phenyl-pent-1-
en-3-ol 3a (40 mg, 92%) as a colorless sticky oil. The enantiometric
selectivity (13.2:1) of 3a in the presence of sulfonamide ligand 8b was
determined from 1H NMR analysis of its (+)-Mosher ester. yield 79%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, yield depends on amt. of cat.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
