$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (b) Typical Procedure for the Addition in
THF-d8. To 1 mL of 1.5 M PhLi in THF-d8 99% was added 66 mg (0.5 mmol) of
(E)-cinnamaldehyde, and the mixtures was allowed to react for 7 h and
then quenched with excess of D2O. The organic layer was dried with
Na2SO4, and a determination procedure similar to that described in (a)
above gave 70% yield of compound 5a-d3. (E)-1-Phenyl-2-penten-1-ol (3c).
Oil. Yield: 71%. Compound 4c: 5%, Compound No: 5c, yield: 24%. 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.01 (t, 3H, J= 7.4 Hz), 2.08 (m, 2H), 5.17 (d, 1H, J=
6.8 Hz), 5.67 (ddt, 1H,J= 1.6, 6.8 and 15.5 Hz), 5.81 (dt, 1H, J= 6.0 and
15.5 Hz), 7.27 (m, 1H), 7.36 (m, 4H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 13.30,
25.19, 75.26, 126.16, 127.49, 128.46, 131.34, 134.31, 143.45. HRMS m/z
for C11H14O calcd 162.1045, found 162.1049.
