$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 1q was prepared via a three-step sequence from
trans-cinnamaldehyde. To a 250 mL round-bottomed flask was added THF (60
mL) and trans-cinnamaldehyde (3.15 mL, 25 mmol). The solution was cooled
down to -78 °C and Iso-propylmagnesium chloride (20 mL, ca. 2.0 M in THF)
was added drop-wise, causing the yellow color to become a dark amber
color. After stirring for 20 min. at - 78 °C the reaction mixture was
warmed up to room temperature which was monitored by TLC. After
completion, the reaction was quenched by drop-wise addition of saturated
ammonium chloride solution (4 mL) followed by distilled water (300 mL).
The organic phase was separated, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
diethyl ether (3 × 400 mL). The combined organic layers dried with
anhydrous sodium sulfate. Gravity filtration followed by concentration in
vacuo afforded the crude allylic alcohol as yellow oil (82%, 3.61 g).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indium-promoted chemo- and diastereoselective allylation of α,β-epoxy
ketones with potassium allyltrifluoroborate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
