$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Racemic Picolinates 6−8 and 13.
2-Methyl-7-phenylhept-2-en-4-yl Picolinate (6). To an ice-cold solution
of 3-methyl-2-butenal (19) (1.14 g, 13.6 mmol) in THF (60 mL) was added
Ph(CH2)3MgCl (26.5 mL, 0.77 M in THF, 20.4 mmol). The solution was
stirred at rt for 2 h and saturated NH4Cl and EtOAc were added with
vigorous stirring. The organic layer was separated and the aqueous layer
was extracted with EtOAc twice. The combined extracts were dried over
MgSO4, washed with brine and concentrated to afford a residue, which was
purified by chromatography on silica gel with hexane/EtOAc to furnish
alcohol 17 Colorless oil, (2.49 g, 90%). IR (neat) 3361, 1453, 748, 699
cm−1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.28−1.34 (m, 1 H), 1.42−1.54 (m, 1 H),
1.55−1.74 (m, 2 H), 1.67 (d, J = 1 Hz, 3 H), 1.72 (d, J = 1 Hz, 3 H),
2.63 (t, J = 7 Hz, 2 H), 4.35 (dt, J = 8, 6 Hz, 1 H), 5.15 (dm, J = 9 Hz,
1 H), 7.14−7.21 (m, 3 H), 7.25−7.31 (m, 2 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
18.3 (+), 25.9 (+), 27.4 (−), 36.0 (−), 37.4 (−), 68.6 (+), 125.8 (+),
128.2 (+), 128.4 (+), 128.5 (+), 135.4 (−), 142.5 (−); HRMS (EI) calcd
for C14H20O (M+) 204.1514, found 204.1516.
