$DATUM 108559-64-4
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Rhodium-Catalyzed Reductive Allylation of
Conjugated Aldehydes with Allyl Acetate. A glass liner containing the
substrate (2 mmol), [Rh(TMEDA)(CO)2][RhCl2(CO)2] (5 mol %), Cs2CO3 nH2O
(2 mmol), allyl acetate (8 mmol) and THF (10 mL) was placed in a 45 mL
autoclave equipped with a magnetic stirring bar. The autoclave was
flushed three times with carbon monoxide and then pressurized to 10 bar.
The autoclave was placed in an oil bath preset to 100°C (110°C)* on a
stirring hot plate. After 24 h (72 h)*, the autoclave was removed from
the oil bath and cooled to room temperature prior to the release of CO
gas. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuum, and the residue was
purified by flash chromatography using 20% of ethyl acetate in hexanes as
eluant to afford the product. 1-Phenyl-3-buten-1-ol (3a)3: The crude
compound was purified by flash chromatography with 20% of EtOAc in
hexanes used as eluant to obtain the title compound as a pale-yellow oil
in 87% yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm 2.32 (bs, 1H), 2.50 (m, 2H), 4.70 (dd,
J = 5.9, J = 7.16, 1H), 5.14 (m, 2H), 5.79 (m, 1H), 7.4 (m, 1H), 7.31 (m,
4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ ppm 43.67, 73.23, 118.17, 125.75, 127.41, 128.29,
134.39, 143.82; m/z (EI) 148 ([M]+ 0.6%), 130 (4), 107 ([M - C3H5]+ 100),
79 (52), 77 (42).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study (optimized on catalysts, bases, carbon monoxide
concentrations)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhodium-Catalyzed Reductive Allylation of Conjugated Aldehydes with Allyl
Acetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Vasylyev, Maksym; Alper, Howard
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(8), 2710-2713

