$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In an one-compartment cell fitted with a
nickel sponge as the cathode (20 cm2) and a stainless steel rod (Fe/Cr/Ni
72/18/10) as the anode was introduced DMF (40 mL) as solvent, NBu4BF4
(0.2 g 0.6 mmol) as supporting electrolyte, and CH2Br-CH2Br (220 μL 2.5
mmol). The preelectrolysis was run under argon, at 18/10, corresponding
to 0.52 mmol of chromium (7%) and 0.26 mmol of nickel (3.5%). entry 4, 78
% alcohol.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
