$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Phenyl-3-buten-1-ol (representative procedure): A mixture of benzaldehyde
(530 mg, 5.0 mmol), allyl bromide (0.88 g, 8 mmol) and stannous chloride
(2.25 g, 10 mmol) in water (10 mL) was stirred in a 10 mL round bottom
flask cell equipped with paired graphite electrode at room temperature.
The suspension was electrolyzed at constant potential (2.0 v) on a
graphite anode (dia. 6 mm) and a graphite cathode (dia. 6 mm) and was
stirred alternately until benzaldehyde was transformed throughly with the
reaction time 6-10 h (or 2 F mol-1 of current was consumed under 100 mA
constant current with the electrolysis time 2-3 h). Afterwards, the
reaction mixture was extracted with ether (3×25 mL). The combined organic
layers were dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate and the organic solvent
was removed on a rotary evaporator. The residue afforded the
corresponding homoallylic alcohols with sufficient purity as judged by
TLC and1H NMR without the need for further purification.
1-Phenyl-3-buten-1-ol. 1H NMR (300Hz, CDCl3): δ 2.49-2.57 (m, 2H),
2.64-2.72 (br, 1H), 4.71 (t, J=6.06 Hz, 1H), 5.12-5.25 (m, 2H), 5.77-5.91
(m, 1H), 7.25-7.44 (m, 5H). 13C HMR (75Hz, CDCl3): δ 43.6, 73.4, 117.9,
125.9, 127.4, 128.3, 134.6, 144.0. IR (film): 3385, 3075, 1641 cm-1.
GC-HRMS (EI) calc. for C10H10 (M+-H2O) 130.0783, found 130.0769.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
