$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol In analogy to a procedure of Münstedt et al.[5]
magnesium turnings (14.0 g, 0.58 mol) were mixed with Et2O (50 mL) and
allyl bromide (ca. 2 mL) was added until the reaction started. Then a
mixture of allyl bromide (43.2 mL, 0.50 mol) and benzaldehyde (38.4 mL,
0.38 mol) in Et2O (100 mL) was slowly added. The reaction mixture was
stirred at room temperature for 1 h and then heated to reflux for another
3 h. Ice (50 g) was added and the resulting suspension was dissolved with
HCl (6 M). The organic layer was separated, washed with aqueous NaHSO3,
aqueous NaHCO3 and H2O, and dried (MgSO4). Evaporation of the solvent and
distillation at reduced pressure (bp. 82 °C / 2.7 mbar) afforded the
desired product as a colourless liquid (47 g, 84 %). 1H-NMR (200 MHz): δ
= 7.40-7.35 (m, 5 H), 5.94-5.74 (m, 1 H), 5.14-5.02 (m, 2 H), 4.72 (dd, J
= 6.0, 3.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.58-2.50 (m, 2 H), 2.31 (br s, 1 H, OH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Cyclization Reactions of IBX-Generated Alkoxyamidyl
Radicals
