$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A for the cross-metathesis of
β,γ-unsaturated ketones: A resealable reaction tube, fitted with a
magnetic follower, was charged with Zhan 1B catalyst (3 - 8 mol%). The
tube was then sealed with a rubber septum and purged with argon. Argon
sparged CH2Cl2 (0.10 M with respect to the β,γ-unsaturated ketone
employed), the appropriate α,β-enone (500 mol%), and the corresponding
β,γ-unsaturated ketone (100 mol%) were added sequentially via syringe.
The rubber septum was then replaced with a screw cap and the tube was
heated at 55 °C (oil bath temperature) for 48 hours. After cooling to
room temperature, the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo.
Purification of the residue by flash column chromatography (FCC), under
the conditions noted, afforded the corresponding α,β-unsaturated
1,5-dicarbonyl. 1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (14) General Procedure A:
Benzaldehyde (500 μL, 4.93 mmol) and allylbromide (200 mol%) were used.
Purification by FCC (petrol-Et2O 4:1) afforded the homoallylic alcohol 14
(548 mg, 75%) as a clear oil. 1HNMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 7.45-7.33 (3H, m),
7.32-7.22 (2H, m),5.90-5.75 (1H, m), 5.23-5.10 (2H, m), 4.84-4.73 (1H,
m), 2.61-2.45 (2H, m), 2.24-2.13 (1H, s). 13CNMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) 143.9,
134.5, 128.4, 127.6, 125.8, 118.4, 73.3, 43.8.
