$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative Procedure for the NHK Reaction of Allyl Halides with
Aldehydes 25 Catalyzed by (+)-12: To an oven dried vial were added
molecular sieves (3 Å), Mn powder (325 mesh, 21 mg, 0.38 mmol) and a
catalytic amount of chromium complex (+)-12 (8.3 mg, 12.61 μmol, 10 mol%)
and the vial was flushed with argon for 15 min. To the mixture was added
anhydrous THF (1 mL) and the resulting brown suspension was stirred at
room temperature for 2 h. The suspension was treated with allyl bromide
or chloride (0.19 mmol) and the mixture was stirred for 1 h. To this
mixture was added neat aldehyde 25 (0.12 mmol) and TMSCl (24 μL, 0.19
mmol) at the temperature specified in Table 3 and the mixture was stirred
at that temperature for the specified length of time. The reaction was
quenched with saturated NaHCO3 solution (1 mL), volatiles were removed in
vacuo, and the residue was extracted with ether (2 x 10 mL). The extract
was washed with brine (20 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated under
reduced pressure, and the resulting crude silyl ether was treated with
aqueous HCl (1M, 2 mL, 2 mmol) in THF (2 mL) at room temperature until
desilylation was complete by TLC. The mixture was diluted with Et2O (20
mL), and the solution was washed with brine (20 mL), dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude residue was purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (30% hexane/ether). The enantiomeric
excess of the pure product was determined by HPLC on a Daicel Chiralcel
OD column. (S)-1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (28a) Colorless oil: 89% ee
[Chiralcel OD, hexane:i-propanol 99:1, 0.5 mL/min tR (minor) 36.2 min, tR
(major) 43.2 min]; [α]D 20 - 52.4 (c 0.1, CH2Cl2), [lit.12 for (R)
enantiomer [α]D 22 + 56.5° (c 1.0, benzene, 95% ee)]; IR (neat) 3356,
3069, 3027, 2922, 2848, 1637, 1603, 1459, 1377, 1357, 1280, 1112, 1046,
910, 758, 700 cm-1; 1H NMR (700 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.07 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H),
2.50 - 2.59 (m, 2H), 4.77 (dt, J = 6.4, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 5.16 - 5.72 (m, 2H),
5.84 (ddt, J = 17.2, 10.0, 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.31 (m, 1H), 7.37 - 7.40 (m,
4H); 13C NMR (175 MHz, CDCl3) δ 43.9, 73.3, 118.5, 125.8, 127.6, 128.4,
134.5, 143.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, yield and ee depend pn temp. and time, molecular sieves
used
