$DATUM 12125-02-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Allylation of Aldehydes 2a-k. An oven-dried 50
mL round-bottomed flask was cooled under argon and charged with
(1S,2R)-(+)-2-amino-1,2-diphenylethanol (2 mmol), indium powder (2 mmol),
anhydrous THF (14 mL), anhydrous pyridine (2 mmol), and allyl bromide (2
mmol). The mixture was stirred vigorously at 25 °C for 30 min, at which
time n-hexane (2 mL) was added, the solution was cooled to-78 °C (dry
ice/acetone bath), and freshly distilled aldehyde (1 mmol) was added
dropwise. After 2 h the reaction was quenched with saturated ammonium
chloride (2 mL) and allowed to warm to 25 °C . Deionized water was added
and the mixture was extracted with n-hexane (2 x 5 mL), then the combined
organic layers were dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate, filtered
through a small plug of silica gel, and evaporated to give the alcohol
product as an oil. 1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol, 2a (Table 2, entry 1).
Following the general procedure above, 2a was obtained as a clear,
colorless oil (0.134 g, 90% yield). 1H NMR (250 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.22 (s,
1H, OH), 2.51 (t, J = 7 Hz, 2H), 4.72 (t, J = 7 Hz, 1H), 5.12-5.20 (m,
1H), 5.73-5.87 (m, 1H), 7.25-7.37 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (62.9 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
43.7, 73.3, 118.3, 125.8, 127.5, 128.3, 134.4, 143.8. Enantiomeric excess
was determined to be 93% by chiral GC analysis. GC conditions: 121 °C
isothermal, tR for the (R)-alcohol = 43.10 min, and tR for the
(S)-alcohol = 43.69 min. The absolute stereochemistry was determined by
comparison of the sign of optical rotation with reported literature
values, [α]25 D = +48.67 (c 0.42, benzene).1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimized on reagent, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Indium-Mediated Asymmetric Barbier-Type Allylations: Additions to
Aldehydes and Ketones and Mechanistic Investigation of the Organoindium
Reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Haddad, Terra D.; Hirayama, Lacie C.; Singaram, Bakthan
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(3), 642-649

