$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Reaction of
Allyltrichlorosilane (2) and Crotyltrichlorosilane (18/19) with
Aldehydes. Allyltrichlorosilane (0.47 mmol) or crotyltrichlorosilane
(0.47 mmol) was added to a solution of the catalyst (0.04 mmol),
diisopropylethylamine (2 mmol) and aldehyde (0.4 mmol) in dichloromethane
(2 mL) or chloroform (2 mL), or acetonitrile (2 mL) under nitrogen at the
specified of temperature (see Table 1). The mixture was stirred at the
same temperature for 18 h and then quenched with aqueous satd. NaHCO3 (1
mL). The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 10 mL) and
the combined organic extracts were washed with brine and dried over
Na2SO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo and he residue was purified by
flash chromatography on a silica gel column (15 cm x 1 cm) with a
petroleum ether-ethyl acetate mixture (95:5). The isolated yields and ee
are given in Table 1. The enantiopurity of the resulting alcohol was
determined by chiral GC, using a Supelco β-DEX 120 column, unless
specified otherwise (see below). (S)-(-)-1-Phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol
(S)-(-)-(3a):4,6 1H-NMR δ 2.08 (s, 1H), 2.37-2.49 (m, 2H), 4.62-4.66 (m,
1H), 5.05-5.15 (m, 2H), 5.68-5.78 (m, 1H), 7.17-7.29 (m, 5H);
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
