$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for catalyzed allylation: Synthesis of
1-phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (Table 2, entry 1). In a glove box, a 20-mL
scintillation vial equipped with a Teflon-coated stir bar and a rubber
septum was charged with (IPr)CuF (22.4 mg, 0.047 mmol) and anhydrous THF
(4.0 mL). The vial was then taken out of the glove box and sealed with
electrical tape. Octyltrifluorosilane (19.0 mg, 0.096 mmol) and
allyltrimethoxysilane (229.1 mg, 1.41 mmol) were added to the solution by
syringe and the mixture was stirred for 5 min. Benzaldehyde (100 mg,
0.942 mmol), previously redistilled to remove traces of benzoic acid, was
added to the solution and the mixture was stirred for 48 h. The reaction
was then quenched with aq HCl (0.1 mL, 2 N soln) and stirred for 1 h.
Ether (15 mL) was added, and the mixture was washed with water (2 × 50
mL) and brine (50 mL). The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated under vacuum. Kügelrohr distillation (chamber at 100 °C, 15
torr) of the residue afforded the final product (113 mg, 81%) as a
colorless oil. Spectral data is consistent with that previously
reported.6 GC/MS, m/z: tR = 7.89 min; [M]+ calcd, 148.2; found, 148.1; (>
95%).
