$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative Allylboration of aldehydes
using Brown’s B-allyldiisopinocampheylborane: Preparation of
4-(1-Hydroxy-but-3-enyl)-benzoic acid methyl ester (4f). All glassware
was oven-dried at 150°C overnight prior to use. A ChemGlass AIRRRFREE®
filter tube was fitted with a three-neck, 100mL round-bottom flask and a
stir bar at both ends. The entire apparatus was placed in an inert
atmosphere glove box and charged with (-)Ipc2BOMe (6.2g, 19.63mmol) and
reassembled prior to removal from the glove box. The solid (-)Ipc2BOMe
was dissolved in dry Et2O (15mL) and cooled to 0°C with stirring.
AllylMgBr (19.6mL, 1M in Et2O) was added dropwise over 20 min along the
inside of the cooled flask. The resulting white suspension was warmed to
room temperature and stirred for 1h. The ether was then removed under
high vacuum and the pasty white salts were redissolved in freshly
distilled pentane (20mL). The filter tube was slowly inverted and then
positive pressure applied to aid in filtration. The salts were washed
with pentane (2 ×20mL) and then the solvent was removed under high
vacuum. The flask was purged with N2 and Et2O (35mL) was added. The flask
now charged with “salt free” allylborane and ether was cooled to -100°C
in a MeOH/N2 (liq.) bath. Aldehyde 3f was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (17mL) and
added very slowly drop-wise along the inside of the flask to cool the
solution. The reaction was monitored by UV TLC analysis (no stain, UV
light, Rf = 0.60; 1:1 hexanes:EtOAc) for completion and warmed to room
temperature once complete. The solution was quenched with a solution of
2N NaOH (10mL) and 30% H2O2 (20mL) and stirred vigorously. The biphasic
mixture was fitted with a reflux condenser and spontaneously began to
reflux after 5 min. Once the reaction slowed, it was warmed to 50°C and
slightly refluxed for 3-5h. The mixture was then extracted with Et2O (3
×20mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solution was filtered, concentrated and
dissolved in hexanes. Biotage chromatography on silica gel (10:1
hexanes/Et2O then 7:1 hexanes/Et2O) provided the pale yellow oil 4f (2.0
g, 70%). Spectral data for 4f below. 4-(1-Hydroxy-but-3-enyl)-benzoic
acid methyl ester (4f): 1-Phenyl-but-3-en-1-ol (4d): 4d was isolated in
76% yield as a clear, colorless oil.
