$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of l Ipc2Ball (3.91 g, 12 mmol) in ether (25 mL) at -100 °C
was slowly added via a cannula a solution of benzaldehyde (1.02 mL, 10
mmol) in ether (20 mL). After 1 h of stirring at -100 °C, the reaction
mixture was quenched with methanol (1 mL). The resulting mixture was then
allowed to warm to room temperature and extracted with 1 N aqueous HCl.
The combined aqueous layers were treated with 30% aqueous NaOH solution
until pH 12-13, and then extracted with CH2Cl2 (4×). The combined
extracts were dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. Purification by flash chromatography gave 4 (1.26 g, 85%) as a
pale yellow oil: 95% ee, determined by chiral HPLC (hexane/i- PrOH )
99/1, 25.0 min for (R)-alcohol and 31.7 min for (S)- alcohol);
(1R)-1-Phenylbut-3-en-1-ol (4) [α]20 D = +44 (c 1.1, benzene) [lit.44
[α]20 D = -44.92 (c 7.38, benzene)]; IR (KBr) ν 1641, 2980, 3075, 3380
cm-1; 1H NMR δ (ppm) 2.04 (s br, 1H), 2.49-2.57 (m, 2H), 4.75 (dd, 1H, J
= 5.9 Hz, J = 7.2 Hz), 5.13 (s, 1H), 5.18-5.23 (m, 1H), 5.73- 5.94 (m,
1H), 7.27-7.39 (m, 5H); 13C NMR δ (ppm) 43.4, 73.3, 117.7, 125.7, 127.2,
128.1, 134.3, 143.8; MS (CI/NH3) m/z 148 (M+), 166 (M + NH +).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Highly Stereoselective Asymmetric Synthesis of (-)-Lobeline and
(-)-Sedamine
